NORMATIVE per-kind layout that `schema_sha256` is computed over. The tool name is the lock's own key and the description is hashed separately, so neither appears here. Keys are always present, with null where the source has nothing, so an addition later is visible as drift rather than as a differently-shaped object.

mcp     -> {"input": inputSchema|null, "output": outputSchema|null}
openai  -> {"input": parameters|null, "output": null}
openapi -> {"method": string, "path": string, "parameters": [...], "requestBody": schema|null, "responses": schema|null}

For `openapi` the fragments are the DEREFERENCED ones the projection actually read: hashing the operation as written would miss a #/components/schemas target changing underneath an unchanged $ref.
